## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of identity-based security, secret management, and infrastructure as code in a beginner Azure context, with emphasis on environment isolation, governance, and CI/CD integration.

## Key Concepts
- Managed identities and Key Vault access policies
- Environment isolation with separate Key Vaults
- Tagging governance and policy enforcement
- Bicep/ARM IaC deployment and GitHub Actions

## Code Example

```bicep
// Minimal example showing a Function App identity and Key Vault access
resource kv 'Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults@2021-04-01-preview' = {
  name: 'kv-${environment}'
  location: resourceGroup.location
  properties: {
    tenantId: subscription().tenantId
    sku: {
      family: 'A'
      name: 'standard'
    }
    accessPolicies: [
      {
        tenantId: subscription().tenantId
        objectId: functionIdentity.properties.principalId
        permissions: {
          secrets: [
            'get'
            'list'
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
    tags: {
      Environment: environment
      Project: projectName
      Owner: ownerTag
    }
  }
}

resource functionIdentity 'Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/userAssignedIdentities@2023-01-31' = {
  name: 'func-identity-${environment}'
  location: resourceGroup.location
  tags: {
    Environment: environment
    Project: projectName
  }
}

resource functionApp 'Microsoft.Web/sites@2022-03-01' = {
  name: 'func-${environment}'
  location: resourceGroup.location
  kind: 'functionapp'
  identity: {
    type: 'UserAssigned'
    userAssignedIdentities: {
      '${functionIdentity.id}': {}
    }
  }
  properties: {
    serverFarmId: appServicePlan.id
    siteConfig: {
      appSettings: [
        {
          name: 'KEY_VAULT_NAME'
          value: kv.name
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  tags: {
    Environment: environment
    Project: projectName
  }
}
```

## GitHub Actions Workflow

```yaml
name: Deploy Azure Resources

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  workflow_dispatch:

env:
  ENVIRONMENT: ${{ github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' && 'prod' || 'dev' }}

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      id-token: write
      contents: read
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Azure Login
        uses: azure/login@v1
        with:
          client-id: ${{ secrets.AZURE_CLIENT_ID }}
          tenant-id: ${{ secrets.AZURE_TENANT_ID }}
          subscription-id: ${{ secrets.AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID }}

      - name: Deploy Bicep
        uses: azure/arm-deploy@v1
        with:
          resourceGroupName: rg-${{ env.ENVIRONMENT }}
          template: main.bicep
          parameters: environment=${{ env.ENVIRONMENT }} projectName=myapp ownerTag=team-email

      - name: Deploy Function Code
        uses: Azure/functions-action@v1
        with:
          app-name: func-${{ env.ENVIRONMENT }}
          package: function-app/
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question introduces a data-analytics angle (ADLS Gen2 + Data Explorer) and governance concerns not covered by prior prompts. It tests knowledge of data flows, security, and cost controls without overloading a single service.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 ingestion patterns
- Azure Data Explorer (Kusto) for dashboards
- Event-driven integration (Event Grid)
- TLS termination and Front Door
- GitHub Actions CI/CD
- Resource tagging and budget alerts
- Lightweight disaster recovery

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: Function writes raw feedback to ADLS Gen2 using @azure/storage-blob
const { BlobServiceClient } = require("@azure/storage-blob");
module.exports = async function(context, req) {
  const blobClient = BlobServiceClient.fromConnectionString(process.env.AZURE_STORAGE_CONNECTION_STRING);
  const container = blobClient.getContainerClient("raw-feedback");
  const blockBlob = container.getBlockBlobClient(`${Date.now()}-feedback.json`);
  await blockBlob.upload(JSON.stringify(req.body), Buffer.byteLength(JSON.stringify(req.body)));
  return { status: 200, body: "ok" };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle schema evolution for feedback records?
- What are the latency and pricing trade-offs between ADLS Gen2 vs Data Explorer ingestion?
- How would you implement data retention and access controls?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical knowledge of observability in a beginner Azure stack, ensuring the candidate can wire instrumentation, telemetry exports, and basic dashboards end-to-end.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry integration in Azure Functions
- Application Insights exporter and per-endpoint metrics
- Sampling, traces, and dashboards in Azure Monitor
- GitHub Actions CI/CD for deployments
- Front Door TLS endpoint configuration
- SQL Auto Failover Group for cross-region DR

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal OpenTelemetry setup (Node.js)
const { NodeSDK } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-node');
const { getNodeAutoInstrumentations } = require('@opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node');
const { AzureMonitorTraceExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-azure-monitor');

const sdk = new NodeSDK({
  traceExporter: new AzureMonitorTraceExporter({
    connectionString: process.env.APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING
  }),
  instrumentations: [getNodeAutoInstrumentations()],
  sampler: new AlwaysParentSampler(0.2) // 20% sampling
});

sdk.start();
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes ability to design end-to-end scalable ingestion with strong isolation and cost discipline, plus onboarding automation.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation strategies (namespaces, resource groups)
- Ingestion options (IoT Hub vs Event Hubs) and scaling
- Data encryption with CMK and Key Vault
- RBAC, Service Principals, least privilege
- Onboarding automation (ARM/Bicep/Terraform), CI/CD
- Monitoring, auditing, budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo onboarding snippet (illustrative only)
async function onboardTenant(tenantId){
  await createEventHubNamespace(`tenant-${tenantId}-eh`);
  await createStorageAccount(`tenant${tenantId}sa`);
  await assignRBAC(tenantId, 'Contributor');
  await configureCMK(`tenant-${tenantId}-cmk`);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test isolation boundaries at scale?
- What are the trade-offs of per-tenant storage vs a shared data lake with tagging?

